# AI Chat API Rules

This rule file defines all the business rules, constraints, and guidelines for the AI Chat API located in [aiChatAPI.js](mdc:backend/controllers/aiChatAPI.js).

## Core API Rules

### 1. Rate Limiting Rules
- **Free Tier**: 10 messages per day, resets every 24 hours
- **Premium Tier**: Unlimited messages
- Counter is database-backed and survives server restarts
- Reset happens automatically when 24 hours have passed since last reset

### 2. Authentication Rules
- JWT authentication is REQUIRED for all chat endpoints
- Guest access is NOT allowed
- Token must be in format: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- Subscription status must be verified for tier determination

### 3. Message Validation Rules
- Messages are REQUIRED and cannot be empty
- Minimum length: 1 character
- Maximum length: 2000 characters
- Only string type is allowed
- Whitespace is automatically trimmed

### 4. Session Management Rules
- Session IDs are optional (auto-generated if not provided)
- Format: `chat_session_<timestamp>_<random>`
- Maximum history length: 20 messages (keeps last 20)
- History is persisted to Pinecone
- In-memory cache used for active sessions

### 5. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Rules
- RAG is ENABLED by default
- Top 5 most relevant chunks are retrieved
- Minimum similarity score: 0.5
- Free tier users are RESTRICTED to knowledge base queries only
- If no relevant context found for free users, block the request

### 6. AI Model Rules
- Provider: Groq
- Model: llama-3.3-70b-versatile
- Temperature: 0.5 (balanced creativity/accuracy)
- Max tokens: 500 per response
- Timeout: 30 seconds maximum

### 7. Response Format Rules
- Format: JSON
- Include metadata by default
- Include session ID in response
- Markdown is supported in responses
- Maximum 2 retries on failure

### 8. Error Handling Rules
- All errors are logged
- Detailed error messages in development mode only
- Production uses sanitized error messages
- Fallback response: "I apologize, but I'm having trouble processing your request right now."

### 9. Content Policy Rules
- Moderation is enabled
- Harmful content is blocked
- Profanity is allowed (not blocked)
- Violations are logged for review

## User Tier Differences

### Free Tier
- 10 messages per day
- Knowledge base queries ONLY
- Cannot ask general questions
- System prompt restricts to company information
- Blocked if query is outside knowledge base

### Premium Tier
- Unlimited messages
- Full AI capabilities
- Can ask any question (AI, tech, general knowledge)
- System prompt allows broad assistance
- No knowledge base restrictions

## API Endpoints

The following endpoints are defined in [aiChatAPI.js](mdc:backend/controllers/aiChatAPI.js):

1. **POST /api/v1/ai-chat** - Main chat endpoint
2. **POST /api/v1/ai-chat/clear** - Clear chat history
3. **GET /api/v1/ai-chat/history/:sessionId** - Get conversation history
4. **GET /api/v1/ai-chat/rules** - Get API rules (for debugging)

## Integration Requirements

When integrating this API, you MUST:

1. Include valid JWT token in Authorization header
2. Validate message before sending (1-2000 chars)
3. Handle rate limit errors (429 status)
4. Handle authentication errors (401 status)
5. Store and reuse session IDs for conversation continuity
6. Handle timeout errors gracefully

## Code Standards

When modifying [aiChatAPI.js](mdc:backend/controllers/aiChatAPI.js):

- All rules must be defined in the `API_RULES` object
- Use helper functions for rule validation
- Log all significant events with emoji prefixes (🤖, ✅, ❌, etc.)
- Include detailed comments for each rule section
- Return consistent JSON error format
- Always save messages to Pinecone for persistence
- Update in-memory cache after each message

## Error Codes

The API uses these standard error codes:

- `AUTH_REQUIRED` - Authentication is missing or invalid
- `INVALID_MESSAGE` - Message validation failed
- `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` - Daily message limit reached
- `AI_ERROR` - AI model generation failed
- `SERVER_ERROR` - Internal server error
- `MISSING_SESSION_ID` - Session ID required but not provided
- `CLEAR_ERROR` - Failed to clear chat history
- `FETCH_ERROR` - Failed to fetch chat history

## Testing

When testing the AI Chat API:

1. Test rate limiting by sending 11 messages (free tier)
2. Test knowledge base restriction with general questions (free tier)
3. Test session persistence by refreshing and loading history
4. Test message validation with empty and long messages
5. Test authentication by sending requests without token
6. Test error handling by causing timeouts or invalid requests

## Performance Targets

- Response time: 1-3 seconds for typical requests
- Cache hit rate: >80% for active sessions
- RAG context retrieval: <500ms
- Message persistence: <200ms (async, doesn't block response)
- History loading: <500ms

## Security Considerations

- Never expose API keys to frontend
- Always verify JWT tokens on every request
- Sanitize error messages in production
- Log all authentication failures
- Rate limiting prevents abuse
- Subscription verification prevents unauthorized premium access

## Dependencies

The AI Chat API depends on:

- [helper.js](mdc:backend/utils/helper.js) - Embeddings and LLM setup
- MongoDB - User data and rate limiting counters
- Pinecone - Vector storage and RAG context
- Groq SDK - AI inference with Llama 3.3
- JWT - Authentication tokens

